    "title": "BTS comeback: Bright lights and drone shows light up the sky as 'Arirang' finally arrives — as it happened",
    "text": "And that's a wrap.Keep on swimming everyone.104,000 people in attendanceHYBE's official count is 104,000 in attendance tonight, and the Seoul Metropolitan Government have agreed on that number.Ignore the city's earlier 40,000 figure, which perhaps didn't take into account the entire area.And just like that, central Seoul returns to normal(ish).The subways are all up and running (the roads might take a little longer), and Cho Jung-woo reports that the platforms at Seoul Station and Jonggak Station look pretty empty, even inside the trainsARMY continue to clean upGood job everyone, it was immensely fun (it wouldn't have been for many of you though..) watching all this happen (online for two whole days). Thank you 💜Even some of the police coaches have started packing up and heading out of Gwanghwamun Square nowSo far so goodThe exit process was one of the biggest concerns, but so far it appears to be going smoothly, according to our reporters on site, perhaps due to what some may see as overly rigid safety measures by police and officials.Many attendees have walked to Jonggak Station to head home as the nearest stations to Gwanghwamun Square were closed. Some exits there are reportedly closed because of overcrowding. Inside, people are taking turns in an orderly manner under the guidance of police and metro officials.Our resident social butterfly is still out there chatting away (Go home Ji-won. Your shift finished an hour ago!)This time it's Bakhova Nurikamal from KazakhstanHow was the show?“It was so good. It was so exciting, really. I really waited for this moment. I was emotional because, you know, it's my first time seeing them. Even though it was through the screen, I could hear their voice in person. I was so happy. “Favorite song? “I expected to hear the old music, so i like 'Mikrokosmos', and 'Dynamite'. I was like, oh, my God.\" Where are you going now?“I am with my friends and we don't know yet, but we're gonna go eat somewhere around here.”Go home, Ji-won! We appreciate your work (SO MUCH)40 to 42,000 peopleAccording to Seoul City Government's official estimate, and feel free to think of that what you will, the total crowd size in Gwanghwamun today was 40,000 to 42,000 people.",
